{"name":"Gentle Giant","hex":"#b3ebe0","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"gentle giant","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A person or animal of a great size or strength, yet who is of a friendly nature and not aggressive or threatening."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/gentle_giant"}],"entries":[{"title":"Gentle Giant","blocks":[{"text":"Gentle Giant were a British progressive rock band active between 1970 and 1980. They were known for the complexity and sophistication of their music and for the varied musical skills of the members. All of the band members were multi-instrumentalists. Although not commercially successful, the band achieved a cult following."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5a/Gentle_giant_1977_press_photo.jpg/330px-Gentle_giant_1977_press_photo.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gentle_Giant","wikidata":"Q943241"},{"title":"Gentle Giant (album)","blocks":[{"text":"Gentle Giant is the debut album by the British progressive rock band Gentle Giant, released in 1970."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/a/a1/Gentlegiantcover.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gentle_Giant_(album)","wikidata":"Q1931594"},{"title":"Giant","blocks":[{"text":"In folklore, giants are beings of humanoid appearance, but are at times prodigious in size and strength or bear an otherwise notable appearance. The word giant is first attested in 1297 from Robert of Gloucester's chronicle. It is derived from the Gigantes of Greek mythology."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/07/Rhinegold_and_the_Valkyries_p_032.jpg/330px-Rhinegold_and_the_Valkyries_p_032.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Giant","wikidata":"Q3707571"}],"imag